{"step_index":55,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-22T11:31:00Z","thinking":"**Analyzing the Request**\n\nOkay, I'm now dissecting the user's prompt. The core is filtering for *famous* places and implementing more animations. My focus is narrowing to the critical component, which is extracting the specific list of famous places. This information will inform the code that I generate. After that, I will work on the animation aspect.\n\n\n**Refining the Focus**\n\nI've streamlined the focus to be exclusively on famous destinations, eliminating any elements related to \"underrated\" places. Furthermore, I've started fleshing out the animations that I will add to the website, particularly within the hero section, destination cards and the interactive destination carousel. The next step is to further refine these animations and consider the implementation specifics.\n\n\n**Developing the Animations**\n\nI'm now fully immersed in the animation specifics. I'm prioritizing smooth transitions for tab switching and category filters, aiming for a spring-like reorganization of items. I'm also planning multi-layer parallax effects for section headings and background watermarks, along with a smooth progress bar. Interactive map pin animations with bounce, glow, and ripple effects are also in the works. Finally, I'm concentrating on the visual flow of modal transitions and engaging counter animations.\n\n\n**Listing the Destinations**\n\nI've completed the collection of the famous destinations. I have a comprehensive and categorized list now. This list is neatly organized. It includes diverse sites from waterfalls and parks to temples and hills. With this, I can begin to refine the code I plan to create.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"/**\n * Jharkhand Tourism - Destination Dataset\n * Curated exclusively for Jharkhand's FAMOUS DESTINATIONS\n */\n\nconst FAMOUS_DESTINATIONS = [\n  {\n    id: \"hundru-falls\",\n    name: \"Hundru Falls\",\n    tagline: \"The 98-meter roaring cascade of Subarnarekha\",\n    category: \"Waterfall & Adventure\",\n    district: \"Ranchi\",\n    location: \"Purulia Road, 45 km from Ranchi\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.4475,\n      lng: 85.6558\n    },\n    elevation: \"320 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"October to March (Post-Monsoon)\",\n    timings: \"06:00 AM - 05:00 PM\",\n    entryFee: \"₹10 per person\",\n    heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1546548970-71785318a17b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1546548970-71785318a17b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1546548970-71785318a17b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1432405972618-c60b0225b8f9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1507525428034-b723cf961d3e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Hundru Falls is one of the grandest natural spectacles in eastern India. Created by the Subarnarekha River plunging 98 meters (322 ft) over a jagged cliff face, it carves magnificent rock formations and natural bathing pools at its base. The descent of over 750 stone steps brings travellers right into the mist and roar of the water.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"98-meter vertical plunge onto sculpted basalt rocks\",\n      \"Natural pools suitable for wading during winter months\",\n      \"Scenic 750-step trail through lush Sal forest canopy\",\n      \"Spectacular rock erosion sculpting million-year geologies\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Birsa Munda Airport Ranchi (48 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Ranchi Railway Station (42 km) or Muri Junction (30 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Well-connected via NH-33 and Purulia Road with taxi and bus services\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Wear shoes with deep rubber tread; stairs and rocks near the plunge pool are permanently wet with fine algae spray.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Strictly avoid swimming near the base during monsoons (July-Sept) due to unpredictable flash currents and submerged whirlpools.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"The Subarnarekha ('Streak of Gold') river was named because ancient villagers panned fine gold dust from its sandy riverbeds.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"betla-national-park\",\n    name: \"Betla National Park\",\n    tagline: \"Ancient Sal forests, tigers & 16th-century Chero forts\",\n    category: \"Wildlife & Nature\",\n    district: \"Latehar\",\n    location: \"Palamu District border, 160 km from Ranchi\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.8824,\n      lng: 84.1887\n    },\n    elevation: \"350 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"November to April\",\n    timings: \"06:00 AM - 05:30 PM (Safari slots apply)\",\n    entryFee: \"₹100 per person + Safari charges\",\n    heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709268805-4e9042af9f23?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709268805-4e9042af9f23?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709268805-4e9042af9f23?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1534177616072-ef7dc120449d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1575550959106-5a7defe28b56?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\"\n    ],\n    description: \"One of the earliest national parks in India to come under Project Tiger in 1974, Betla spans rolling hills, teak groves, and dense sal forests. Deep inside the jungle stand the mysterious twin 16th-century Palamu Forts built by the sovereign Chero kings, blending royal Mughal-tribal stone architecture with untamed wilderness.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"Elephant-back and 4x4 open safari tracks\",\n      \"Historic 16th-century Chero Dynasty jungle forts\",\n      \"Diverse wildlife: Elephants, leopards, gaur (Indian bison), chital & sloth bears\",\n      \"Lush tropical deciduous vegetation and natural waterholes\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Ranchi Birsa Munda Airport (165 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Daltonganj Railway Station (25 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Regular private and state buses run from Ranchi, Daltonganj, and Netarhat\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Always hire a registered forest department naturalist guide and stay strictly inside safari vehicles on track routes.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Do not venture into fort ruins on foot without forest rangers; wild elephants and sloth bears frequent the forest corridor after sunset.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"Betla's name is an acronym: B-Bison, E-Elephant, T-Tiger, L-Leopard, A-Axis axis (Chital).\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"patratu-valley\",\n    name: \"Patratu Valley & Lake\",\n    tagline: \"Serpentine ribbon roads and emerald reservoir waters\",\n    category: \"Scenic & Lakes\",\n    district: \"Ramgarh\",\n    location: \"Ramgarh-Ranchi Highway, 35 km from Ranchi\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.6358,\n      lng: 85.2986\n    },\n    elevation: \"410 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"September to March\",\n    timings: \"Open 24 Hours (Best during daylight & sunset)\",\n    entryFee: \"Free (Boating charges apply at Patratu Lake Resort)\",\n    heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506744038136-46273834b3fb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506744038136-46273834b3fb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506744038136-46273834b3fb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1469854523086-cc02fe5d8800?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1510312305653-8ed496efae75?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Often celebrated as the 'Queen of Highways in East India', Patratu Valley unfolds along mesmerizing hairpin switchbacks carved across steep forested hills. At the valley floor rests the vast Patratu Dam & Reservoir, offering speedboating, island cafes, and sunset promenades that rival international lakeside getaways.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"Thrilling multi-tiered winding ghat road with panoramic viewpoints\",\n      \"Watersports: Jet ski, pontoon boats, and speedboats on Patratu Lake\",\n      \"Spectacular twilight valley illuminated by solar ribbon lamps\",\n      \"Modern waterfront promenade and island restaurants\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Birsa Munda Airport Ranchi (40 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Patratu Railway Station (5 km) or Ranchi (35 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Pithoria-Patratu 4-lane scenic highway is an effortless 50-minute drive from Ranchi\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Exercise low gears and respect speed limits on the hairpin bends, especially in dense morning winter fog.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Avoid stopping or parking your vehicle on sharp blind curves along the ghat for photography.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"The serpentine road has over 30 distinct hairpin turns, making it a favorite drive for motoring clubs across Eastern India.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"parasnath-hill\",\n    name: \"Parasnath Hill (Shikharji)\",\n    tagline: \"The supreme sanctum on Jharkhand's highest peak (1,365m)\",\n    category: \"Mountain Peaks\",\n    district: \"Giridih\",\n    location: \"Parasnath, Giridih District\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.9628,\n      lng: 86.1333\n    },\n    elevation: \"1,365 m (4,478 ft)\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"October to March\",\n    timings: \"04:00 AM - 07:00 PM\",\n    entryFee: \"Free\",\n    heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1464822759023-fed622ff2c3b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1464822759023-fed622ff2c3b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1464822759023-fed622ff2c3b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1519681393784-d120267933ba?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Rising dramatically above the Chotanagpur Plateau to 1,365 meters, Parasnath Hill is the highest mountain summit in Jharkhand. Revered as Shri Sammed Shikharji, 20 of the 24 Jain Tirthankaras attained Moksha (salvation) here. The 27-km pilgrimage circumambulation trail leads through misty cloud forests and ancient marble shrines.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"Highest peak in Jharkhand offering 360-degree panoramic horizons\",\n      \"Sacred cluster of 31 ancient Jain temples crowning ridges and peaks\",\n      \"27-km scenic hiking circuit through biodiverse montane forest\",\n      \"Sunrise viewpoint offering sea-of-clouds vistas in winter\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Kazi Nazrul Islam Airport Durgapur (140 km) or Ranchi (160 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Parasnath Railway Station (PNME) (22 km from base town Madhuban)\",\n      byRoad: \"Located right off Grand Trunk Road (NH-19) with frequent transport from Dhanbad and Ranchi\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Begin the 27-km ascent before dawn (4:00 AM) with ample water, energy snacks, and trekking sticks.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Respect the religious sanctuary sanctity: non-vegetarian food, alcohol, and leather items are strictly prohibited across the holy hill.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"Twenty Jain Tirthankaras, including Parshvanatha after whom the hill is named, attained Nirvana upon these very ridges.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"baidyanath-dham\",\n    name: \"Baba Baidyanath Dham\",\n    tagline: \"One of India's 12 revered Jyotirlingas & Shakti Peeth\",\n    category: \"Spiritual & Heritage\",\n    district: \"Deoghar\",\n    location: \"Deoghar City\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 24.4925,\n      lng: 86.7001\n    },\n    elevation: \"254 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"September to March (Sultanganj Kanwar Yatra occurs in Shravan)\",\n    timings: \"04:00 AM - 09:00 PM\",\n    entryFee: \"Free (VIP Darshan passes available)\",\n    heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1582510003544-4d00b7f74220?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1582510003544-4d00b7f74220?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1582510003544-4d00b7f74220?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544735716-392fe2489ffa?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Baba Baidyanath Temple complex in Deoghar is a rare confluence where a sacred Shiva Jyotirlinga and a Shakti Peeth (Hridaya Peeth) reside in adjacent sanctums. The main 72-foot stone spire features a Panchasula (five-pronged trident) and is the destination for millions during the legendary 105-km barefoot Kanwar pilgrimage.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"Ancient main stone sanctum housing the sacred Kamana Linga\",\n      \"Cluster of 21 auxiliary temples dedicated to diverse Vedic deities\",\n      \"Rare Panchasula trident crowning the stone shikhar\",\n      \"Epic spiritual energy during the sacred month of Shravana\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Deoghar International Airport (DGH) (8 km from temple)\",\n      byTrain: \"Jasidih Junction (JSME) (8 km) - major mainline railway hub\",\n      byRoad: \"Direct NH routes connect Deoghar with Patna, Ranchi, Kolkata, and Bhagalpur\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Keep valuables secure in cloakrooms; use official digital e-pass queues during high festival periods.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Avoid unauthorized middlemen outside temple gates; follow official temple trust queues exclusively.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"Unlike other Shiva temples which have a Trishula (3 prongs), Baidyanath temple has a rare Panchasula (5 prongs) atop its spire.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"jonha-falls\",\n    name: \"Jonha Falls (Gautamdhara)\",\n    tagline: \"Hanging valley cascade where Lord Buddha rested\",\n    category: \"Waterfall & Adventure\",\n    district: \"Ranchi\",\n    location: \"Jonha, 40 km East of Ranchi\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.3444,\n      lng: 85.6072\n    },\n    elevation: \"290 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"October to February\",\n    timings: \"06:00 AM - 05:00 PM\",\n    entryFee: \"₹10 per person\",\n    heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1432405972618-c60b0225b8f9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1432405972618-c60b0225b8f9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1432405972618-c60b0225b8f9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1507525428034-b723cf961d3e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Also called Gautamdhara, Jonha Falls is a classic hanging valley waterfall created where the Raru River drops 43 meters to join the main plateau basin. A tranquil Buddhist shrine sits above the 722 stone steps, commemorating the belief that Gautama Buddha bathed here during his journeys across Magadha.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"43-meter hanging valley waterfall surrounded by forested knolls\",\n      \"Historical Buddhist Ashram and shrine on the upper cliff\",\n      \"Spectacular rock pools and broad stepping stones\",\n      \"Picturesque weekly tribal haat (market) on Tuesdays and Saturdays\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Birsa Munda Airport Ranchi (42 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Jonha Railway Station (1.5 km) or Ranchi Junction (40 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"40 km drive via Ranchi-Purulia highway with scenic forest stretches\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Take breaks when climbing back up the 722 stone stairs; keep hydration handy.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Do not climb onto the slippery rock ledges directly beside the upper fall crest.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"Jonha is an example of an edge knickpoint waterfall created by geological rejuvenation of the Chotanagpur river system.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"dassam-falls\",\n    name: \"Dassam Falls\",\n    tagline: \"Ten torrential streams plummeting into Kanchi gorge\",\n    category: \"Waterfall & Adventure\",\n    district: \"Ranchi\",\n    location: \"Taimara village, 34 km from Ranchi\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.1436,\n      lng: 85.4667\n    },\n    elevation: \"310 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"October to March\",\n    timings: \"08:00 AM - 05:00 PM\",\n    entryFee: \"₹15 per person\",\n    heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1546548970-71785318a17b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1546548970-71785318a17b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1546548970-71785318a17b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1432405972618-c60b0225b8f9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Originally known as 'Da-song' in the local Mundari tribal dialect ('Da' meaning water, 'Song' meaning pouring out), Dassam Falls drops 44 meters over sheer granite cliffs. The Kanchi River splits into ten distinct sparkling streams before roaring into a deep forested canyon.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"44-meter natural cascade splitting into ten distinct streams\",\n      \"Glass skywalk & newly built cantilevered viewing bridges\",\n      \"Dramatic acoustic echo through the canyon amphitheatre\",\n      \"Surrounding virgin Sal and Mahua woodland trails\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Ranchi Airport (35 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Ranchi Junction (34 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Smooth drive along Ranchi-Tata Highway (NH-33) turning right at Taimara\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Stay behind the designated stainless steel safety railing and glass viewpoints at all times.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Swimming or bathing in the plunge pool is strictly prohibited; the underwater current has hidden cavernous under-tows.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"The name Dassam is a corruption of the Mundari phrase 'Da-Song' referring to 10 cascading streams.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"netarhat\",\n    name: \"Netarhat (Queen of Chotanagpur)\",\n    tagline: \"The famous hill station crowned in mist, pine & legendary sunrises\",\n    category: \"Mountain Peaks\",\n    district: \"Latehar\",\n    location: \"Western Plateau, 154 km from Ranchi\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.4833,\n      lng: 84.2667\n    },\n    elevation: \"1,128 m (3,700 ft)\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"Year-Round (Best Oct - March for clear sunrises)\",\n    timings: \"Open 24 Hours\",\n    entryFee: \"Free\",\n    heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506744038136-46273834b3fb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506744038136-46273834b3fb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506744038136-46273834b3fb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1511497584788-87676104235f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1470071459604-3b5ec3a7fe05?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Perched atop an expansive flat laterite plateau at 1,128 meters, Netarhat is the undisputed 'Queen of Chotanagpur'. Celebrated for its crisp alpine weather, fragrant British pine plantations, and the iconic Magnolia Sunset Point, it is Jharkhand's premier hill destination.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"Magnolia Point: Famous sunset overlooking the vast Koel River valley\",\n      \"Pine forest walks with morning mist and fresh mountain resin\",\n      \"Upper & Lower Ghaghri waterfalls nestled in Sal forests\",\n      \"Cool hill climate with winter temperatures touching near freezing\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Ranchi Birsa Munda Airport (154 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Lohardaga Railway Station (85 km) or Ranchi (154 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Mesmerizing hill drive from Ranchi through Lohardaga with scenic forested ghats\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Carry warm woollens between November and February as temperatures drop sharply after sunset.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Avoid driving through isolated forest ghat sections late at night; plan your mountain transit during daylight hours.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"The British named it 'Nature's Hat' due to its bowl-shaped plateau topography, which evolved into Netarhat.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"lodh-falls\",\n    name: \"Lodh Falls (Burha Ghaag)\",\n    tagline: \"The highest waterfall in Jharkhand (143 meters)\",\n    category: \"Waterfall & Adventure\",\n    district: \"Latehar\",\n    location: \"Near Mahuadanr, 195 km from Ranchi\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.5500,\n      lng: 84.0500\n    },\n    elevation: \"450 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"September to February\",\n    timings: \"08:00 AM - 04:30 PM\",\n    entryFee: \"₹10 per person\",\n    heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1432405972618-c60b0225b8f9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1432405972618-c60b0225b8f9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1432405972618-c60b0225b8f9?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1546548970-71785318a17b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Tumbling from a staggering height of 143 meters (469 feet) across multiple stepped tiers on the Burha River, Lodh Falls is the 21st highest waterfall in India and the highest in Jharkhand. Enveloped by pristine forests, its acoustic rumble echoes for miles.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"Highest waterfall in Jharkhand with a 143-meter multi-tiered plunge\",\n      \"Natural amphitheater surrounded by primeval Sal forests\",\n      \"Pristine ecotourism sanctuary with rich birdlife and orchids\",\n      \"Iconic thunderous roar heard from kilometers away\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Ranchi Airport (195 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Daltonganj Railway Station (120 km) or Latehar (90 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Accessible via Mahuadanr valley road from Netarhat (60 km) or Daltonganj\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Fuel up your vehicle completely before leaving Mahuadanr or Netarhat; no fuel stations on interior forest tracks.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Do not attempt to cross river rapids or climb upper tiers; water surge is powerful and swift.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"The acoustic rumble of Lodh Falls is so powerful in peak flow that locals call it 'The Thunder of Chotanagpur'.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"dalma-wildlife-sanctuary\",\n    name: \"Dalma Wildlife Sanctuary\",\n    tagline: \"Hilltop elephant sanctuary overlooking Jamshedpur\",\n    category: \"Wildlife & Nature\",\n    district: \"East Singhbhum\",\n    location: \"Dalma Hills, 10 km from Jamshedpur\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 22.9000,\n      lng: 86.2167\n    },\n    elevation: \"926 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"October to April\",\n    timings: \"07:00 AM - 05:00 PM\",\n    entryFee: \"₹50 per person + Vehicle pass\",\n    heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709268805-4e9042af9f23?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709268805-4e9042af9f23?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709268805-4e9042af9f23?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506744038136-46273834b3fb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Spread over 195 sq km across the Dalma mountain range towering 926 meters high, this sanctuary is famous for its resident Asian elephant population, barking deer, leopards, and ancient hilltop Shiva temple. The viewpoint at the summit provides breathtaking vistas of Jamshedpur glowing beside the Subarnarekha River.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"Dalma Summit Viewpoint with panoramic 360-degree plains views\",\n      \"Natural elephant habitat and canopy bird observation towers\",\n      \"Hilltop Shiva temple visited by forest pilgrims for generations\",\n      \"Pindrabera Forest Rest House perched above the valley\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Ranchi Birsa Munda Airport (125 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Tatanagar Junction Jamshedpur (18 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Smoothly accessible from NH-33 just 10 km north of Jamshedpur city\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Carry binoculars and drive under 20 km/h inside sanctuary limits to avoid startling wildlife.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Entry is closed after 5:00 PM; strictly adhere to ranger instructions regarding elephant herd movements.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"During the annual Sendra festival, tribal trackers traverse these hills in a tradition that predates modern recorded history.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"tagore-hill\",\n    name: \"Tagore Hill (Morabadi)\",\n    tagline: \"The philosopher's hill of the Tagore family in Ranchi\",\n    category: \"Spiritual & Heritage\",\n    district: \"Ranchi\",\n    location: \"Morabadi, Ranchi City\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.4022,\n      lng: 85.3356\n    },\n    elevation: \"650 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"October to March (Mesmerizing at Sunrise/Sunset)\",\n    timings: \"06:00 AM - 06:30 PM\",\n    entryFee: \"₹10 per person\",\n    heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513694203232-719a280e022f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513694203232-719a280e022f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513694203232-719a280e022f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1506744038136-46273834b3fb?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Rising 300 feet above the Ranchi plateau in Morabadi, Tagore Hill was the cherished sanctuary of Jyotirindranath Tagore (elder brother of Rabindranath Tagore). Here, atop the granite knoll, he built 'Shanti Dham' in 1908 and translated celebrated philosophical classics in total contemplation.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"Shanti Dham: Historic stone pavilion perched at the rocky peak\",\n      \"Brahmo Mandir and Tagore Art & Cultural exhibition museum\",\n      \"Sweeping panoramic vistas over Ranchi city and Morabadi grounds\",\n      \"Peaceful shaded stone pathways perfect for contemplative walks\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Birsa Munda Airport Ranchi (12 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Ranchi Railway Station (7 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Centrally situated in Morabadi, easily accessible by auto-rickshaw or taxi\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Take care when stepping on open granite surfaces during wet monsoon showers.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Do not climb beyond designated boundary walls or railings on the cliff overlook.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"Rabindranath Tagore visited his brother here and drew deep inspiration from the Chotanagpur forest landscape for parts of 'Gitanjali'.\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"maithon-dam\",\n    name: \"Maithon Dam & Lake\",\n    tagline: \"The serene 'Mother's Abode' with blue water islands and speedboating\",\n    category: \"Scenic & Lakes\",\n    district: \"Dhanbad\",\n    location: \"Barakar River, 48 km from Dhanbad\",\n    coordinates: {\n      lat: 23.7844,\n      lng: 86.8153\n    },\n    elevation: \"156 m\",\n    bestTimeToVisit: \"October to March\",\n    timings: \"06:00 AM - 06:00 PM\",\n    entryFee: \"Free (Boating charges apply)\",\n    heroImage: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1507525428034-b723cf961d3e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=80\",\n    thumbnail: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1507525428034-b723cf961d3e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=80\",\n    gallery: [\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1507525428034-b723cf961d3e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\",\n      \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1469854523086-cc02fe5d8800?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=80\"\n    ],\n    description: \"Built over the Barakar River, Maithon ('Mai-ka-than' or Mother's Abode) features a massive 65-square-kilometer blue reservoir dotted with green islands, an underground power station, and the ancient Kalyaneshwari Temple.\",\n    highlights: [\n      \"65 sq km blue water lake with speedboating to Sabuj Dweep (Green Island)\",\n      \"India's first unique underground hydel power station\",\n      \"Centuries-old sacred Kalyaneshwari Temple located nearby\",\n      \"Picturesque sunrise and sunset views over tranquil reservoir waters\"\n    ],\n    howToReach: {\n      byAir: \"Kazi Nazrul Islam Airport Durgapur (60 km)\",\n      byTrain: \"Kumardhubi Station (5 km) or Dhanbad Junction (45 km)\",\n      byRoad: \"Conveniently located 8 km off the Grand Trunk Road (NH-19)\"\n    },\n    safety: {\n      precaution: \"Always wear life jackets provided during boat rides across the deep reservoir channels.\",\n      majorWarning: \"Strictly avoid venturing close to spillway gates and intake towers where strong suction currents operate.\"\n    },\n    funFact: \"Maithon Dam was inaugurated by Prime Minister Jawaharlal Nehru in 1957 as part of the historic Damodar Valley Project.\"\n  }\n];\n\n// Curated Informational Micro-Moments (\"Did You Know?\" editorial facts)\nconst DID_YOU_KNOW_FACTS = [\n  {\n    number: \"01\",\n    tag: \"ETYMOLOGY & NATURE\",\n    headline: \"Jharkhand literally means 'The Territory of Forests'\",\n    body: \"Derived from 'Jhar' (dense forest/bushland) and 'Khand' (land), over 29% of the state's geographical area is enveloped in primeval Sal, Mahua, and Teak woodland canopy.\"\n  },\n  {\n    number: \"02\",\n    tag: \"INDIGENOUS HERITAGE\",\n    headline: \"Home to 32 Unique Indigenous Tribal Communities\",\n    body: \"Rich in living ancestral wisdom, Jharkhand's Santhal, Munda, Oraon, Ho, and Birhor tribes maintain continuous thousand-year traditions in harmony with Mother Nature (Marang Buru).\"\n  },\n  {\n    number: \"03\",\n    tag: \"LIVING ART FORMS\",\n    headline: \"GI-Tagged Sohrai & Khovar Murals Painted with Natural Earth\",\n    body: \"Tribal women paint intricate ritual wall art using naturally sourced manganese black, ochre yellow, and white kaolin clay, a tradition dating back to prehistoric rock art.\"\n  },\n  {\n    number: \"04\",\n    tag: \"GEOLOGICAL WONDERS\",\n    headline: \"The Chotanagpur Plateau is over 2.5 Billion Years Old\",\n    body: \"Part of the ancient Gondwanaland supercontinent, this dramatic plateau features stepped knickpoints creating dozens of pristine waterfalls cascading across ancient granite.\"\n  }\n];\n\n// Travel Themes for Experience Showcase\nconst TRAVEL_THEMES = [\n  {\n    id: \"waterfalls\",\n    title: \"Roaring Waterfalls & Canyons\",\n    subtitle: \"From 143-meter thunderous plunges to serene emerald pools\",\n    count: \"15+ Cascades\",\n    image: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1546548970-71785318a17b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=80\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"wilderness\",\n    title: \"Untamed Wildlife & Sal Forests\",\n    subtitle: \"Asia's densest Sal reserves, wild elephant herds and tigers\",\n    count: \"4 Sanctuaries\",\n    image: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518709268805-4e9042af9f23?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=80\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"spiritual\",\n    title: \"Sacred Summits & Ancient Shrines\",\n    subtitle: \"Revered Jyotirlingas, Jain mountain peaks, and timeless pilgrimages\",\n    count: \"8 Holy Sites\",\n    image: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1582510003544-4d00b7f74220?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=80\"\n  },\n  {\n    id: \"culture\",\n    title: \"Tribal Arts, Music & Living Traditions\",\n    subtitle: \"Sohrai murals, Dokra metalcraft, and vibrant seasonal harvest rhythms\",\n    count: \"32 Cultures\",\n    image: \"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1513694203232-719a280e022f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=80\"\n  }\n];\n","Description":"Update data.js to focus exclusively on famous destinations with rich photography and safety information","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\Bhavish Sawant\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\jharkhand-tourism\\js\\data.js","toolAction":"Updating data.js","toolSummary":"Updating data.js"}}]}
